<title>USA: Strike avoided at GM's Delphi Lighting plant.</title>
<headline>Strike avoided at GM's Delphi Lighting plant.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at General Motors' Delphi Interior and Lighting plant in Anderson, Indiana, reached a tentative labor pact early Wednesday, a spokeswoman for Delphi said.</p>
<p>The company had received a five-day letter notifying GM that UAW Local 663 was planning to strike if an agreement was not reached.</p>
<p>The union represents 2,380 workers at the plant, the spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said she did not know when the union plans to hold a ratification vote.</p>
</text>
